
# Week 3 — Transfer Learning and Model Improvement

## What Was Done

During Week 3, the baseline CNN model from Week 2 was improved using transfer learning and regularization techniques.

Completed tasks:

* Implemented Transfer Learning using MobileNetV2
* Added data augmentation:

  * RandomFlip
  * RandomRotation
  * RandomZoom
* Added Dropout layers to reduce overfitting
* Built a new training pipeline with pretrained feature extraction
* Compared results with the baseline CNN model
* Generated updated accuracy curves

---

# Dataset

| Property                 | Value                                             |
| ------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------- |
| Dataset                  | Intel Image Classification                        |
| Total images             | ~25,000                                           |
| Classes                  | 6                                                 |
| Categories               | buildings, forest, glacier, mountain, sea, street |
| Image size               | 150×150                                           |
| Train / Validation split | 80% / 20%                                         |

Dataset source:
[Intel Image Classification Dataset](https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/puneet6060/intel-image-classification?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

---

# Augmentation Applied

The following augmentation techniques were added to improve generalization:

* Random horizontal flip
* Random rotation (±10%)
* Random zoom

These methods helped reduce overfitting and improved validation performance.

---

# Model Architecture

Input: 150 × 150 × 3

```text id="arch"
Image
→ Data Augmentation
→ Rescaling
→ MobileNetV2 (pretrained on ImageNet)
→ GlobalAveragePooling2D
→ Dropout(0.3)
→ Dense(128, ReLU)
→ Dropout(0.3)
→ Dense(6, Softmax)
```

Transfer learning was implemented using MobileNetV2 with frozen pretrained weights.

---

# Training Configuration

| Parameter      | Value                           |
| -------------- | ------------------------------- |
